        <body>
            <div xml:id="d996">

                <pb facs="0670" n="598" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg598"/>

                <head>Inhabitants of St. Maurice</head>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">St. Maurice</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-12">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 12, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. President</hi>: The eminent man who fell by the
                    murderous hand of the infamous villain Booth, at the moment his soul winged its
                    flight to the celestial regions, left regrets and profound grief in our hearts.
                    The atrocious crime of which Mr. Abraham Lincoln was the victim has filled us
                    with indignation and horror.</p>
                <p>We regret the great loss to the North—the loss of a great, generous, and
                    noble-heart, who did so much for the abolition of slavery, for all his aims were
                    to do good to his fellow-man. Yet we hope that the Americans of the North will
                    finish the great work of the noble martyr, whose motto was, “<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Liberty, equality and fraternity</hi>.</p>
                <p>Such is the sincere wish of the undersigned citizens of St. Maurice.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>HENRY GARNY,</item>
                            <item>THOS. PRUDE,</item>
                            <item>ALBERT DEBONNAIRE,</item>
                            <item>ANTOINE DUTART,</item>
                            <item>FRANCOIS GEX,</item>
                            <item>PHILIBERT CHEVALLIER,</item>
                            <item>LOUIS SEYDOUX,</item>
                            <item>FRANCOIS BURNIER,</item>
                            <item>LOUIS SARRASIN,</item>
                            <item>F. GAY,</item>
                            <item>CHARLES VOEFFRAY,</item>
                            <item>JOSEPH DUBOULE,</item>
                            <item>JOS. MEIZOZ,</item>
                            <item>PIERRE DUFOUR,<lb/>And several others.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
